{\pard\sb120\sa60\sl360\slmult1
{\b\f0\fs28\cf5 3.4 Lessons on Method\par}
}

{\pard\sb60\sa60\sl360\slmult1\f0\fs22\cf1
\bullet\tab {\b Sample rate matters.} 5 s samples understated peaks by up to ~0.4 GB; transient problems need 1 s or better.\line
\bullet\tab {\b Separate 'settled' from 'peak'.} A flat settled level looked like 'no leak' while the peak was the real risk; the same chart read by eye looked like a leak when the growth was small.\line
\bullet\tab {\b Compare against a clean baseline.} The first load from the main menu (from 1.2 GB) was the control that showed the peak is the load's own cost, not something left over from the previous flight.\line
\bullet\tab {\b Use the engine's own counters with care.} The census's texture total (~22 GB) is an RGBA32 estimate because the release player reports 0 for Profiler sizes; Texture.currentTextureMemory (3.7-4.1 GB) is the reliable figure.\line
\bullet\tab {\b One stall is still unexplained.} The 19:41 stall happened at only 6.7 GB, so not every failure is VRAM exhaustion.\par}

